$title { Notes on MathML }

$og_description { Notes on typesetting mathematics in the browser }

[class=blog-content]{

h1[class=center | style=font-size: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; overflow: visible; ] { Notes on MathML }

h2[class=center | style=font-size: 0.7rem; ]{⸺ how to render beautiful math in the browser ⸺}



math-style: normal;

font-size: math;

font-family

the only font that i have found to produce adequate typesetting in browser mathml is Latin Modern Math. i have a fairly strict policy, in developing this site of mine, of not pulling in external dependencies beyond what is provided by the browser itself. the one exemption i have granted myself to this, at time of writing, is that my site serves Latin Modern Math as a .woff2; the mathematical typesetting cannot be brought up to my standards without it.


}


